    "title": "Concept 1: Speed",
    "explanation": "<p class=\"text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">Speed is a compound measure that tells us how fast something is moving. It is calculated by dividing the distance travelled by the time taken. The formula is: <strong>Speed = Distance &divide; Time</strong>. Common units are metres per second (m/s), kilometres per hour (km/h), and miles per hour (mph).</p>",
