    "title": "Concept 2: Density",
    "explanation": "<p class=\"text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">Density measures how much mass is packed into a given volume. It is calculated using the formula: <strong>Density = Mass &divide; Volume</strong>. Common units include grams per cubic centimetre (g/cm³) and kilograms per cubic metre (kg/m³).</p>",
